    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d280">

                <pb facs="0398" n="226" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg226"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/3264</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mooney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Asuncion</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-08T16:00:00-03:50">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 8, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 9, 1.45
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s February 3, 1 p.m. The Paraguayan Minister for Foreign Affairs has
                    privately informed me that he is in full sympathy <pb facs="0399" n="227"
                        xml:id="pg227"/> with the position of the United States. The Paraguayan
                    Government has not yet taken action on the question and having but little
                    interest in sea commerce may abstain from formally expressing its attitude.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mooney</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
